fwtrial host bundle: deploy a recording node, record, check
==========================================================

Everything runs from this directory. Node: root@10.42.0.132 below; use yours.
Nothing here builds code; the node software is the fwtrial-*-aarch64.tar.gz
next to this file. Version: see VERSION.

Laptop needs (Ubuntu 24.04, x86_64)
-----------------------------------
  sudo apt install openssh-client curl ffmpeg libcurl4t64

  SSH key login to the node as root:   ssh-copy-id root@10.42.0.132
  (after the board's SD card was reflashed:   ssh-keygen -R 10.42.0.132)

1. Check this laptop and the link (read-only; says what is missing and how to fix it)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  bin/fwt-doctor host root@10.42.0.132
  bin/fwt-doctor dev root@10.42.0.132      the node itself (encoder, /rec, services, PTP)

  OK / WARN (works, not as expected) / FAIL (won't work) + "fix:" line.

2. Deploy the node software (starts at boot; recordings in /rec are kept)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ./deploy.sh root@10.42.0.132

  Ends with:   DEPLOYED <version> to root@10.42.0.132
  Back to the previous version:
    ssh root@10.42.0.132 sh /opt/fwtrial/current/install.sh --rollback
  Remove everything but the recordings (refused while recording):
    ./deploy.sh root@10.42.0.132 --uninstall

3. Node status (read-only)
--------------------------
  bin/fwt-rec 10.42.0.132 --info

4. Record
---------
  mkdir -p ~/rec
  bin/fwt-rec 10.42.0.132 --duration 30 --out ~/rec/run1.h265
  bin/fwt-rec 10.42.0.132 --duration 30 --fps 60 --out ~/rec/run2.h265

  Arms a new session, records for the duration (on the node's clock),
  disarms (also on Ctrl-C), fetches the whole session into the file, writes
  FILE.json next to it (node, versions, session, frames, missing) and checks
  the file with sei-dump. Ends with "check: passed ... pixels ok" and "OK".
  Exit code 0 = recorded, nothing missing, check passed.

  Play:   ffplay ~/rec/run1.h265
  Check a file again:   bin/sei-dump -q ~/rec/run1.h265

Problems
--------
  Start with bin/fwt-doctor (step 1). On the node:
    ssh root@10.42.0.132 sh /opt/fwtrial/current/install.sh --status
    ssh root@10.42.0.132 journalctl -u fwtrial-nodeagent -b --no-pager | tail -20
